<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a pallet dispenser?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A pallet dispenser (destacker) automatically separates individual empty pallets from a stack and feeds them to a <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">palletizer conveyor</a>. Eliminates manual pallet placement for continuous palletizer operation.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">Dispenser vs. destacker?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The terms are interchangeable. Both refer to a machine that separates individual pallets from a stack. No industry-standard distinction exists between the two terms.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How many pallets can a dispenser hold?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>It depends on pallet height and the dispenser frame. Whallon, for example, rates its dispenser bin at up to 12 pallets, with extensions available. Multi-stack and inline dispensers hold more. Higher capacity reduces refill frequency for high-speed lines.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What types of pallet dispensers are available?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Magazine-style (single stack, bottom-dispensing, lowest cost), inline (continuous flow, integrates into pallet conveyor, adds conveyor cost), and robotic (handles mixed pallet sizes, recipe-based changeover, highest cost). Magazine-style is most common for standard operations.</p>

</div>
